OL,3,A'Law change will be my sons' legacy - I
OL,4,Ahope they're proud of me'
OL,5,
OL,6,FClaire Throssell missed seeing her sons
OL,7,Fby five minutes. She was on her way
OL,8,Fback from work when they set off for a
OL,9,Fvisit to see their father.
OL,11,FWhen police knocked on her door later
OL,12,Fthat night, her first thought was:
OL,13,F"What has he done?"
OL,15,FHer estranged husband, Darren Sykes,
OL,16,Fhad started a fire in his home while
OL,17,FJack, 12, and Paul, nine, were inside
OL,18,Fthe attic looking at a train set, then
OL,19,Flocked them in.
OL,23,APub: 17-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,311,300,200,140,0,100
